entries.methodology:
An externally built model scores each pitcher's pitch types from TrackMan kinematics against run value, then rescales to a class-relative index. Governance: registry row collegesavant_stuff, eval artifact data/collegesavant_stuff_eval.json: seasons 2024-2026, thousands of pitchers per full season, agreement r 0.96 with the sibling vintage vendored in the repo.

Scale collision: six things here are called some form of Stuff+ and none share a scale:
(1) this CollegeSavant display (college TrackMan xRV ratio, 100 = college average, 0 = worst observed, SD about 23-24);
(2) Will's 2026 formula-anchored vintage (same family, a different fit, vendored separately);
(3) aStuff+ (in-house AAA model, 100 + 10z vs the qualified AAA pool);
(4) tjStuff+ (Thomas Nestico's per-pitch MLB model, 100 minus 10z, clamped 20-180; inverted sign convention);
(5) pStuff+ in Python for the served statline (peripheral K% / BB% / HR-9 vs level, 100 + 10z);
(6) pStuff+ in the PROSPX leaderboard JS (same family, reconciled onto the Python formula 2026-07-29).
A 130 here is barely plus; a 130 aStuff+ is elite. They are never mixed on one surface.

A gated test as a college-to-pro K% translation covariate failed (zero forward signal on 257 matched pairs), so it stays display context.
